# Automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) in front of the SIP management API.
#
# NOT runtime-tested — no Docker daemon was available during development
# (same limitation noted for rtpengine in README.md). Caddy's automatic
# HTTPS is a well-documented, widely-used feature, but verify this
# actually issues a certificate on your VPS before trusting it — if
# {$API_DOMAIN} can't resolve to this VPS's IP over DNS, or ports 80/443
# aren't open, certificate issuance will fail silently-ish and Caddy will
# keep retrying rather than serving your traffic.
#
# Substituted from API_DOMAIN in .env via docker-compose's environment
# variable interpolation (Caddy reads {$VAR} directly, no separate
# templating step needed here, unlike kamailio.cfg).

{$API_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy api:3000
}
